    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e8debd08ad7d1dff97a1067f3684e2fcdf514df1cfca89c53585a490704ea761",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The two short-interval maximum arguments expose opposite one-sided uses of prime-scale paths. For an upper estimate, Cauchy localization and a lossy transfer to a large smooth factor lead to barrier events whose failures are controlled by union bounds and optimized high moments. For a typical-window lower estimate, roughly equal-variance interior prime blocks and a spatial grid lead to a simultaneous high-block event proved by a second-moment argument that controls both far and near pairs.",
