      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ecf0d9667c2d10106ab4e67f40e5dad1e13e3ae10a57afef0447c17b65b81ac9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The cited resonance mechanisms expose two different method-specific bottlenecks. The GCD construction is limited by support capacity together with the available GCD upper bound, whereas monotone extraction in the general resonance lemma requires nonnegative Dirichlet coefficients. For argument observables, imaginary projection is cancellation-sensitive, an off-critical-line zero correction is explicit before RH removes it, and the earlier Cauchy-kernel bridge from log modulus to S1 changes sign and yields only an absolute-value conclusion.",
