      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The squared-modulus short-window integral is a positive local aggregate. One source gives its asymptotic after averaging over height and then poses the distinct question of its typical size; the freezing source varies the exponent beta in a differently normalized fixed-window integral and reports a renormalized numerical free-energy response. The concrete bridge is the beta=1 member of the local partition-mass family, while the mean/typical comparison and the beta-response diagnostic remain different questions.",
